Scoring notes:
\begin{itemize}
\begin{itemize}
\item[-] The first point is earned for \(\int_{0}^{\pi}\left|v_{P}(t)\right| d t\).
\item[-] The first point can also be earned for a sum (or difference) of definite integrals, such as \(\int_{0}^{2.145029} v_{P}(t) d t-\int_{2.145029}^{\pi} v_{P}(t) d t\), provided the response has indicated \(v_{P}(2.145029)=0\).
\item[-] The second point can only be earned for the correct answer.
\item[-] The unsupported value 1.931 earns no points.
\item[-] A response reporting the distance traveled by particle \(Q\) as \(\int_{0}^{\pi}\left|v_{Q}(t)\right| d t=3.506\) earns the first point and is not eligible for the second point.
\item[-] In degree mode, the total distance traveled is 0.122. (See degree mode statement in part (a).) In the degree mode case, the response must present \(\int_{0}^{\pi}\left|v_{P}(t)\right| d t\) in order to earn the first point because \(\int_{0}^{\pi}\left|v_{P}(t)\right| d t=\int_{0}^{\pi} v_{P}(t) d t\).
\end{itemize}
\end{itemize}

